<heading>refine split - Split the current room along a line.</heading>

<rule/>

<heading level="2">
Usage
</heading>

<pre>
refine split ANGLE
refine split ANGLE --offset OFFSET
</pre>

<heading level="2">
Description
</heading>

<paragraph>
Refines the current room into two rooms. The split is a graph
transformation: a second room is created, the halves are connected, and
every endpoint of the current room is reassigned to the half its
orientation falls into. Connections themselves stay unchanged.
</paragraph>

<paragraph>
The angle is measured in the mathematical convention: 0° is east, angles
count counterclockwise. The line always passes through the room's center.
The optional offset (between -1 and 1, default 0) shifts the line along
its normal: 0 is the center, ±1 puts the line on the edge.
</paragraph>

<paragraph>
An endpoint whose orientation lies exactly on the line stays with the
original room.
</paragraph>

<heading level="2">
Examples
</heading>

<pre>
refine split 90
  Split into an upper and a lower room.

refine split 0
  Split into a left and a right room.

refine split 45
  Split diagonally (north-east half becomes the new room).

refine split 0 --offset 0.8
  Split off a narrow strip on the east side.
</pre>

<heading level="2">
See also
</heading>

<paragraph>
dig, connect, box/edit, look
</paragraph>
